# lane E L-c (RELEASE_PLAN step 5; STEP5_PLAN 10, the owner's q14d): THE 9-ROW PAUSE MENU (docs/CUSTOM_FRONTEND.md
# 5.14). Port features on (this recipe); off = the retail menu, untouched.
#   RESUME GAME, RESTART OBJECTIVE, SAVE / LOAD   the game's own btn1-btn3, as they were
#   ACHIEVEMENTS                                  btn4 (was STATISTICS): the host page (SR_Achievements, lane E L-a)
#   STATISTICS, MOVES LIST                        btn5, btn6 (were MOVES LIST, GAMEPLAY OPTIONS): the game's own screens
#   OPTIONS                                       btn7 (was CONTROLLER OPTIONS): the one OPTIONS screen (lane E L-b)
#   (PHOTO MODE)                                  btn8 (was AUDIO OPTIONS): hidden and out of the focus order until
#                                                 unit P gives it its action - its slot is kept, so P needs no layout
#   QUIT GAME                                     btn9: QUIT TO TITLE / QUIT TO DESKTOP (srpause.aptasm ShowQuit)
# No clone: the nine retail buttons are re-labelled and re-purposed, so the tab order (m_tabIndex 0-8) and the game's
# own by-name select / disable / restore (InitGui: RESTART and SAVE / LOAD, PauseSelectedItem) keep their shape.
# The rows sit on one 38-unit pitch from y 68 (ACHIEVEMENTS fills the retail gap after SAVE / LOAD), the QUIT spacer is
# kept: QUIT GAME at 392 (retail 58 .. 344 and 402); the panel, its bevels and the hint bar do not move.
# The MORE OPTIONS row (iter-464 btn10) is gone: what it held is in OPTIONS (AUTOSAVE and, in a dev build, DEV TOOLS on
# the GAME tab; DISPLAY / GRAPHICS / WORLD; CHEATS), MODS is on the MAIN MENU only.
movie SCRPAUSEMENU
edit-place btn1 char=2 y=68
edit-place btn2 char=2 y=106
edit-place btn3 char=2 y=144
edit-place btn4 char=2 y=182
edit-place btn5 char=2 y=220
edit-place btn6 char=2 y=258
edit-place btn7 char=2 y=296
edit-place btn8 char=2 y=334
edit-place btn9 char=2 y=392
append-to action initaction:ScrPauseMenu file=srpause.aptasm
append-to action initaction:BistroBaseScreen file=devtools_ui.aptasm
# InitGui (reg1 this, reg2 _global): after the game's own labels, the re-purposed rows' labels (STATISTICS and MOVES
# LIST in the game's own text, through its LocalizationAdapter; ACHIEVEMENTS and OPTIONS are literals, as MORE
# OPTIONS was), btn8 out of the menu, then SRPause.Install(this)
append-to function InitGui in ScrPauseMenu
    EA_PushConstByte 'ACHIEVEMENTS'
    EA_PushOne
    Push [reg1]
    EA_GetNamedMember 'btn4'
    EA_CallNamedMethodPop 'SetText'
    EA_PushConstByte 'Label_ScrStatistics'
    EA_PushOne
    Push [reg2]
    EA_GetNamedMember 'LocalizationAdapter'
    EA_PushConstByte 'GetLocalizedText'
    CallMethod
    EA_PushOne
    Push [reg1]
    EA_GetNamedMember 'btn5'
    EA_CallNamedMethodPop 'SetText'
    EA_PushConstByte 'Label_ScrMovesList'
    EA_PushOne
    Push [reg2]
    EA_GetNamedMember 'LocalizationAdapter'
    EA_PushConstByte 'GetLocalizedText'
    CallMethod
    EA_PushOne
    Push [reg1]
    EA_GetNamedMember 'btn6'
    EA_CallNamedMethodPop 'SetText'
    EA_PushConstByte 'OPTIONS'
    EA_PushOne
    Push [reg1]
    EA_GetNamedMember 'btn7'
    EA_CallNamedMethodPop 'SetText'
    EA_PushZero
    Push [reg1]
    EA_GetNamedMember 'btn8'
    EA_CallNamedMethodPop 'disable'
    Push [reg1]
    EA_GetNamedMember 'btn8'
    EA_PushConstByte '_visible'
    op_74
    SetMember
    Push [reg1]
    EA_PushOne
    Push [reg2]
    EA_GetNamedMember 'SRPause'
    EA_CallNamedMethodPop 'Install'
end
# HandleInput(keyCode r4): A on a re-purposed row (btn4 ACHIEVEMENTS, btn5 STATISTICS, btn6 MOVES LIST, btn7 OPTIONS,
# btn9 QUIT GAME) does what the game's own rows do first - PauseSelectedItem := the row (the game's own focus restore
# when its screen closes), the button's own press, the OPEN sound - then the row's action (SRPause.OnRow); RESUME,
# RESTART and SAVE / LOAD keep the game's own handling. reg3 / reg5 are the game's own scratch registers here (it
# writes them first thing in its CROSS branch).
prepend-to function HandleInput in ScrPauseMenu
    Push [reg4]
    Push [reg2]
    EA_GetNamedMember 'INPUTCODE'
    EA_GetNamedMember 'CROSS'
    Equals2
    Not
    If pmi_done
    EA_PushZero
    Push [reg2]
    EA_GetNamedMember 'gFM'
    EA_PushConstByte 'getSelectedItem'
    CallMethod
    StoreRegister 5
    Pop
    Push [reg5]
    EA_GetNamedMember '_name'
    StoreRegister 3
    Pop
    Push [reg3]
    EA_PushConstByte 'btn4'
    Equals2
    If pmi_mine
    Push [reg3]
    EA_PushConstByte 'btn5'
    Equals2
    If pmi_mine
    Push [reg3]
    EA_PushConstByte 'btn6'
    Equals2
    If pmi_mine
    Push [reg3]
    EA_PushConstByte 'btn7'
    Equals2
    If pmi_mine
    Push [reg3]
    EA_PushConstByte 'btn9'
    Equals2
    If pmi_mine
    Jump pmi_done
pmi_mine:
    Push [reg2]
    EA_PushConstByte 'PauseSelectedItem'
    Push [reg3]
    SetMember
    Push [reg4]
    EA_PushOne
    Push [reg5]
    EA_CallNamedMethodPop 'handleInput'
    Push [reg2]
    EA_GetNamedMember 'SOUND'
    EA_GetNamedMember 'OPEN'
    EA_PushOne
    Push [reg2]
    EA_CallNamedMethodPop 'playSound'
    Push [reg3]
    EA_PushOne
    Push [reg2]
    EA_GetNamedMember 'SRPause'
    EA_CallNamedMethodPop 'OnRow'
    op_74
    Return
pmi_done:
end
prepend-to function ExitScreen in ScrPauseMenu file=pause_exitscreen_head.aptasm
